		{"id":"4c24dc7c65616b42","type":"group","x":-835,"y":1280,"width":1315,"height":639,"label":"Polperro Law and Cycle of Production"},
		{"id":"ddd0ff8473834286","type":"text","text":"Engine on Astrakahn burns out","x":24,"y":1038,"width":280,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"c2493e695f6b0418","type":"text","text":"Burned engine sent to Crullfeld","x":185,"y":1117,"width":269,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"15cde4a95c4710cf","type":"text","text":"Backup thrusters are monitored","x":204,"y":928,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"4b747929389eb9f9","type":"text","text":"New engines are built","x":-101,"y":958,"width":195,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"3bcf44106dd71fe1","type":"text","text":"Repaired engine sent to Astrakahn","x":-101,"y":1117,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"d06951e292fe4fed","type":"text","text":"Broken engines scrapped","x":-255,"y":1038,"width":239,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"3cabcfa3d034dbc2","type":"text","text":"**Medical Procedure Standards**\nAny procedure done on living or non-living beings must have at least two licensed medical personnel present during the operation.","x":-823,"y":1300,"width":424,"height":125,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"1a0dd7fb77e17f21","type":"text","text":"Damien and Sam are running from police and bump into Chloe","x":4318,"y":-979,"width":250,"height":121},
		{"id":"d5503adfe7ef6336","type":"text","text":"General Story","x":5185,"y":-968,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"3085274e66f049ec","type":"text","text":"Samuel","x":4725,"y":-998,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"b0af872df122c729","type":"text","text":"Elliott","x":5665,"y":-998,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"e9d6f45546b3d544","type":"text","text":"Elliot is autopsicizing a Crullfeld enginner to extract valuable metal from body\n\nAssistant pushes \"is something up with you? you're being sloppy today.\"\n\nElliot starts ripping into the body, slicing frantically, yelling about how it doesnt matter and he's dead anyway.\n\n\"That man had a family, sir.\"\n\n\"If he were more careful, maybe he'd be home with them instead of here on MY TABLE.\" He throws a chunk of metal at the wall next to the assistant.\n\nAssistant is appalled and leaves to get supervisor.\n\nElliot flips over table, body flops on the floor, he's stressed to the maximum.\n\n\"I can't keep doing this kind of grunt work.\" he has a small monologue to himself or something\n\nElliot is taken to the residents office and scolded about his outburst.\n\nElliot reinforces that he could be doing so much more with his skills, which is shut down by \"it doesn't matter what you *can* do if you don't do what you're told first.\"\n\nElliot is suspended from his job for a week. \n\nCut to Elliots morning routine. Get up, get coffee, eat breakfast, talk to the urns of your dead parents, OH FUCK WAIT I'M SUSPENDED!!!\n\nThrows his coffee, almost hits the urns. He apologizes, trying to calm himself down, interrupted by ringtone.\n\n\"Hey we need you down at the Labs, something weird is going on.\" Elliot is instantly calm, it's creepy.\n\nORCUS INTRODUCTION!!! HOLY SHIT!!! THIS IS IMPORTANT!!! LISTEN TO ME!!!\n(Elliot walking with guy while wrapping up suits)\n\nThey captured the guy who blew himself up at the bank. He looks super mutated and weird. He's thrashing in his restraints, trying to get out.\n\n\"WTF is happening WTF is happening get this shit off me.\"","x":5600,"y":-271,"width":392,"height":1310},
		{"id":"69b43575b251e731","type":"text","text":"","x":5600,"y":1122,"width":392,"height":1558},
		{"id":"1cb0f47c0178dd2b","type":"text","text":"Bank robber accidentally blows himself up, exposing the people of Ozryn to Orcus' existence.","x":5178,"y":-858,"width":265,"height":136},
		{"id":"d1b85cbc02d7defc","type":"text","text":"Petty theft before Sam starts climbing Ozryn?","x":4277,"y":-797,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"752e31cfb69ba3d0","type":"text","text":"**Basic Story Events**","x":5185,"y":-1098,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"08caefc6fa35f2e6","type":"text","text":"I blew up\n\nI felt them carry by body onto a gurney. Yes, *felt*. Somehow, despite the explosion, I was still feeling... still breathing...\n\n**Part 1 - Still Living**\nwhat orcus does\nstill image of the lives of the ozryn people\nthat dumbass fly thats somehow still living in my room","x":5238,"y":-1556,"width":462,"height":296},
		{"id":"96ea7b398bd0d34b","type":"text","text":"Sam is packing bags after getting fired. Damien reveals Orcus to Sam, who sees it as all the more reason to start climbing Ozryn. This is where we see the core differences between Sam and Damien. Damien is reluctant and wants to stay where it's safe, Sam drags him along anyway.","x":4080,"y":260,"width":328,"height":248},
		{"id":"00b5414c4ccb1ca4","type":"text","text":"**Alias Gordon**\nManager of Samuels factory. Uptight ass.","x":3220,"y":78,"width":340,"height":69},
		{"id":"ef95f220663e9bf2","type":"text","text":"**Garrison Gallo**\nCaitlin's father. Former president of Ozryn.","x":3220,"y":180,"width":360,"height":69},
		{"id":"c7da260d4c83964a","type":"text","text":"**Damien Skoddie - Crullfeld Propulsion Engine Repairman**\nAge: 20\nBuild: Mesomorph\nCharacter Notes:\n\n-  Hardheaded to a fault\n-  Chokehold greeting type of man\n-  Prioritizes his own well being above all else\n-  Soft spot for his friend Samuel\n\nBackstory to come if it is needed.","x":1940,"y":640,"width":460,"height":320,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"c6015bb48d1607fe","type":"text","text":"**Chloe - Child of Orcus**\nAge: 13\nBuild: Ectomorphic\nCharacter Notes:\n\n-  Deadpan expression, no body language.\n-  Soft spoken, speaks Old English.\n-  Cunning, I guess.\n\nStripped of her identity during her time in the Children of Orcus. Split from the cult partly out of childish rebellion and partly because of flaws she saw in Orcus' rhetoric. Was born into the cult, so she does not have a common name.","x":2900,"y":640,"width":600,"height":320,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"8b2099e7f022b5df","type":"text","text":"**Caitlin Gallo - President of Ozryn**\nAge: 32\nBuild: Mesomorph\nCharacter Notes:\n\n-  Self aware of her own knowledge\n-  Confident in her ability to lead\n-  Wishes to ground Astrakahn for Ozryn's safety.\n\nThrust into position of power after her father fell ill.","x":2420,"y":640,"width":460,"height":320,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"190f22c2c20c227e","type":"text","text":"Its break time at the factory\n\nBreaking news is some dumb fuck blew up\n\nSam walks away with Damien\n\nManager gets onto him for leaving break area\n\n\"I'm going to the bench. Subdue thy breasts.\"\n\nSam and Damien talk, this is their introduction.\n(SAM STEALS A SANDWICH, misses his dad)\n\nDog comes up to bite the sandwich, sam shoos it and it starts whining. Stupid bro sees Sam.\n\n\"Yo is that my fucking sandwich bro?\"\n\nthey fight. afterward, he picks it up, wipes it on his shirt, and keeps eating. \n\nBreak time ends. They're gearing up and getting ready to work again.\n\nBig ozryn exposition while sam and damien talk on the unsafe gondola.\n\nThe pair reach the turbine they're supposed to clean, blah blah a modicum about how they hate Astrakahn then skip to end of work day.\n\nSam says bye to Damien, runs into manager on the way out.\n\n\"Your performance was great, but you followed next to none of the proper safety precautions.\"\n\n\"What safety precautions?\"\n\n\"The same safety precautions that kept your father alive longer, the same ones he ignored.\"\n\nSam gives him an angry glare, clenches his fist, then walks away.\n\n\"Breakin' the cycle, good on you Sammy.\"\n\n\"...The fuck was that?\"\n\n\"Your daddy had a temper too, 'least you're keepin' a cap on it\"\n\nSamuel punches el gordo\n\nwe get the abuse scene(tm)\n","x":4645,"y":-767,"width":392,"height":1194},
		{"id":"0ac9c4bf451772cc","type":"text","text":"Sam comes into work, going to lockers to grab gear.\n\nAs he puts on his rig, manager shows and slams his locker shut.\n\n\"Sammy boy, we need to talk.\"\n\n\"It's with a not so heavy heart that I come bearing your termination letter.\"\n\n\"Wasn't my call, but you still deserve it.\"\n\nSam slaps the letter out of his hand and starts putting on his gear again, manager chuckles. Everyone around them is watching now\n\n\"I'm serious, Solis. You don't want a repeat of yesterday, do ya?\"\n\nSam ignores him and walks past toward the loading dock.\n\nThe manager whistles, and dogs come to bite at Sam's legs. All of the workers around him stay put\n\n\"Get out of here Sammy, you don't work here no more. Hand over your gear.\"\n\nyeah so Sam has to leave, Damien is still at work cus duh so Sam goes home.\n\nWhile Sam is home, we explore his aspirations for the future, he wants to see Astrakahn, but it's obvious that that won't be happening any time soon.\n\nHe comes to the conclusion that he needs to leave Crullfeld and take matters into his own hands. \n\nHe goes out to a market to get some food, but he finds that his units card is not working. He wasn't just fired, he was wiped from the system, he would have to collect his units from the head office.\n\nGuy pays for Sam's sandwiches, citing that he hated what they were doing to him. Sam starts to doubt his decision to leave just a hair.\n\nHe goes back home, and after just getting in the door, Damien comes rushing.\n\nDamien says he wanted to be here asap to check up on him, but Sam isn't having it, and a small argument ensues.\n\nSam's emergency factory alarm goes off. startling the two of them. The voice goes on to explain the surface level details of Orcus, to check local news outlets for more information, to stay safe, and to listen to the orders of the Polperro medical soldiers should they be deployed.\n\nThe pair are both confused. Sam reveals his decision to leave Crullfeld, to which they have a back and forth about it which ultimately ends with Damien agreeing to go with Sam \"so I can keep you out of trouble.\"\n\nSam wonders how that Crullfeld robber got to Polperro, and they conclude it was the maintenance tunnels, they go out to one of the sites and bribe an engineer.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","x":4645,"y":580,"width":392,"height":1740},
		{"id":"e7d6012fd294d16f","type":"text","text":"**Elliott Greene - Polperro Medical Scientist**\nAge: 31\nBuild: Ectomorphic and well fed.\nCharacter Notes:\n- Cold and analytical while absorbed in his work\n- Egotistically enthusiastic about potential discoveries\n- Sociopathic tendencies\n- Holds himself high and stays well kept.\n\nHe watched his parents die at the hands of a domestic terrorist, murdering the perpetrator himself. His perspective on human life has begun to shift toward that of a resource.\n\nWhen given orders to research those afflicted by Orcus, he begins to dissect dead subjects, yearning for a living person to experiment on to potentially find a cure for this cursed immortality.","x":2560,"y":78,"width":600,"height":455,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0a162de0e3ae18be","type":"text","text":"**Samuel Solis - Crullfeld Propulsion Engine Repairman**\nAge: 19\nBuild: Ectomorphic and slightly malnourished.\nCharacter Notes:\n- Stays quiet and relaxed \n- Assesses situations and holds his tongue\n- Internally ambitious, will show interest in something that'll further his goals\n- Soft spot for his friend Damien\n\nHis mother died during childbirth and lost his father in an accident at their assigned propulsion factory. Ever since, he's had aspirations to one day work in Astrakahn and help develop a way to ground the city for good.\n\nUpon learning of the Orcus crisis, he decides to expedite the ascension process and begins to illegally climb Ozryn with his friend Damien.\n\n\n","x":1940,"y":78,"width":600,"height":455,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"1dbda023b953160e","type":"text","text":"Does Orcus only get energy once? How would more be created after revival, since that would \"break the economy\" of Thessara's energy.","x":1448,"y":-213,"width":400,"height":88,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"08ef39bffe6b191d","type":"text","text":"The people of Crullfeld and Polperro work to produce materials to keep Astrakahn afloat, literally. They believe that if you work hard enough, you can ascend the layers and become a resident of Astrakahn.","x":1506,"y":77,"width":309,"height":184,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"b8a686beb3903a15","type":"file","file":"Pasted image 20260512215602.png","x":1409,"y":427,"width":400,"height":196},
		{"id":"9575ddf0faf6f8ea","type":"text","text":"Orcus wants the energy that Thessara uses to grow her creations. Through the Children of Orcus, he promised to grant immortality with the hidden rule that their energy would be given to him instead of Thessara after each death.","x":1497,"y":-484,"width":283,"height":240,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"72705f7e262a72c4","type":"text","text":"**Excrement - Samuel's Archdemon given life**","x":2780,"y":1092,"width":379,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"3fe9ea7857e98cf2","type":"text","text":"**Orcus - The Blight of Chauntea**","x":2400,"y":1092,"width":308,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"1ddb450310cb1af1","type":"text","text":"**Chauntea - Heart of the Planet**","x":1962,"y":1092,"width":338,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"d81775f27ac54a79","type":"text","text":"**Polperro**\n- Steampunk\n- Semi-Wealthy, White Collar","x":1296,"y":297,"width":284,"height":114,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"78497909de339c17","type":"text","text":"**Orcus (Hex)**\nThe brain and heart are scribed with the DNA of a Cambion and programmed to swiftly rebuild itself upon injury. So long as the heart and brain stay mostly intact, a Cambion afflicted with Orcus can be rebuilt.","x":1107,"y":-438,"width":346,"height":216,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"894871239fa02e31","type":"text","text":"**Ozryn (Megacity)**\nOzryn is the capital of Chauntea and the hub of communications for all megacities. It is constructed in a wedding cake style, with each layer becoming smaller, but holding people of higher status.\n","x":1055,"y":38,"width":400,"height":175,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"7d6b272caac40158","type":"text","text":"**Crullfeld**\n- Dieselpunk\n- Lower Class, Blue Collar","x":1001,"y":411,"width":245,"height":126,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"44f3c938d12916a3","type":"text","text":"**Astrakahn**\n- Retrofuturism\n- Investors, Government","x":907,"y":261,"width":241,"height":112,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"4891509de35dd566","type":"text","text":"**Methods of Transport**\nCoils: Public Transit\n- Inside the layers\n- Moves upward and downward mainly\n- Circles the layers and acts like an elevator\n\nFreight Rails: Bulk Goods\n- Outside the layers\n- Moves only upward and downward\n- Set up at \"Shipping Checkpoints\"\n\nAirships: Goods & Transport to Astrakahn\n- One ship at each cardinal direction around the city's perimeter\n- Strategically docked at Crullfeld to bait conflict\n\nMaintenance Tunnels: Illegal Travel\n- Serves the real purpose of getting engineers to places as fast as possible\n- Within the layer walls\n- Engineers can be bribed into giving rides","x":540,"y":627,"width":598,"height":550,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"f25b6a615d13ae1c","type":"text","text":"The False Divine - Name given to Orcus by worshipers of Thessara","x":1497,"y":-619,"width":363,"height":80,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"a33f93674fadbbd0","type":"text","text":"**What is Blue Collar work?**\nThe people of Crullfeld will engineer fuel cells for the propulsion technology of Astrakahn. This is the largest imported resource between the layers. However, Crullfeld and Polperro both handle the bulk of production in general infrastructure, food, goods, and more.","x":540,"y":411,"width":386,"height":207,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"722d695940819d24","type":"text","text":"**Financial System**\nThe entire world of Chauntea, in accordance to Ozryn law, financially operates with the ambiguous \"Unit\" system. One unit is equivalent to one US Dollar.","x":605,"y":4,"width":321,"height":182,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"1b5af1b1540994f2","type":"text","text":"**How do you kill a Hexed Cambion?**\nSince Orcus works from the DNA of the Cambion, continuous mutation would begin to corrupt the data held in a Cambions heart and brain. Once fully transformed into an Archdemon, Orcus no longer has any Cambion DNA to rebuild, which renders it useless.","x":445,"y":-335,"width":507,"height":166,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"8a1ea0a370cf0046","type":"text","text":"**Orcus (Perceived Disease)**\nThessara, upon finding out about the deity Orcus' hex on the Cambion people, was outraged to not have an immediate solution. Eventually, Thessara declared that Cambion may live forever, but must live in her own image. When a hexed Cambion is injured, they will now start to be reconstructed as an Archdemon.\n\nUpon discovery of this genetic mutation, the general populous of Eidolon deemed Orcus a disease.","x":460,"y":-634,"width":476,"height":270,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"94800fd458fa6eba","type":"text","text":"**Orcus (Deity)**\nThe deity of Undeath. Through worship, one can attain immortality. Acts as a foil to the natural order, which the deity Terra despises.","x":1080,"y":-619,"width":400,"height":153,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ead41783919dc3d9","type":"text","text":"**Children of Orcus**\nA cult that worshipped the deity Orcus. Through time, they were manipulated by Orcus to allow his influence into Eidolon, spreading the hex of Orcus.\n\nWhen Orcus learned of Thessara's meddling, Orcus ordered his children to give their final sacrifice in front of the people of Ozryn and the megacities.","x":1060,"y":-962,"width":388,"height":275,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"2ea5c1ba47f1ffd1","type":"text","text":"\"We've been blessed.\"","x":200,"y":172,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0bb907f23606daa9","type":"text","text":"\"I can use this to benefit.\"","x":200,"y":412,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"05b14358750de0b5","type":"text","text":"\"No death means no war.\"","x":200,"y":252,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"07a821eda2d8f349","type":"text","text":"\"This is medically amazing.\"","x":200,"y":332,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"4948647b5de2c6c9","type":"text","text":"**Orcus is Good**","x":140,"y":86,"width":310,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"f090f06bb83d3834","type":"text","text":"Set a scene OUTSIDE of a bar to stab at that one guy that said bar scenes are overused","x":260,"y":-940,"width":273,"height":107},
		{"id":"db81ea48da0ae168","type":"text","text":"**Archdemon**\nThe first of the deity Thessara's creations. They are a fierce race of war bred humanoids that thrived in strategic battle.","x":-89,"y":-330,"width":420,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"e6d8905f99e23514","type":"text","text":"**City Name Ideas**\nAscot\nCrasmere","x":40,"y":-900,"width":281,"height":108},
		{"id":"35f6311a56797065","type":"text","text":"**Cambion**\nThe \"human\" of Eidolon. Through years of technological advancement, their Archdemon bloodlust was quelled.","x":-69,"y":-169,"width":381,"height":151,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"19c4c3bc6a64396c","type":"text","text":"\"We will all become corrupt.\"","x":-160,"y":172,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"d488fabdfd31ec25","type":"text","text":"**Orcus is Bad**","x":-227,"y":86,"width":317,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ea53970d6e028b7a","type":"text","text":"\"Pretend it doesn't exist.\"","x":-160,"y":252,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"5c644b7771b80010","type":"text","text":"\"We've been cursed.\"","x":-160,"y":332,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"8c22ed8ea6763381","type":"text","text":"\"How do we fix this?\"","x":-160,"y":412,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"bf6ad993fbca9cdc","type":"text","text":"**Thessara**\nThessara is a deity that, as she grew, pulled in chunks of inorganic mass from the loose expanse of space pre-civilization. The further seeded into the world she created, the more life sprawled from her essence. ","x":-153,"y":-592,"width":367,"height":187,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"1d71896dc440f0a4","type":"text","text":"**Writing Affirmations**\nI am struggling to add detail to (insert thing)!!!\n |  Extensive detail ≠ depth\nBut what about the rest of the world?\n | Doesn't fucking matter","x":-640,"y":-940,"width":501,"height":163},
		{"id":"24e75b88e1799ea6","type":"text","text":"**Cycle of Energy**\nWhen a lifeform on Eidolon dies, the energy that Thessara used to grow it is absorbed back into Thessara's core for later recycling.","x":-457,"y":-364,"width":331,"height":156,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ab50ab5f810ff99e","type":"text","text":"**Eidolon**\nThe world of Eidolon is similar to that of Earth. Due to the deity living within, it has no core. All resources come from the masses of land that Thessara pulled together.","x":-680,"y":-579,"width":395,"height":161,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"5241715bd65c8b98","type":"text","text":"**The Divide**\nArchdemons, being a war driven species, would often battle with one another over patches of territory, resources, or just for fun. When the discovery of other continents came, a war that shook Eidolon as they knew it erupted, causing a hard divide between massive factions of Archdemons. These ancient settlements eventually grew into the modern day megacities, with social networks being established as the need for war dwindled.","x":-960,"y":-364,"width":470,"height":270,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c9004e0e1c08d541","type":"file","file":"Pasted image 20260106003342.png","x":-960,"y":-583,"width":180,"height":169},
		{"id":"21c1b3e57f017b49","type":"text","text":"**Mandatory Breaks**\nAll employees must take their government mandated breaks at the exact scheduled time. They must stay within the confines of the break area.","x":-823,"y":577,"width":353,"height":159,"color":"3"}
	],
